  m_Name: item_art_a1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::GlorifiedBody.Interaction.ItemDefinition
  itemId: art_a1
  displayName: THE PALMS
  kind: 6
  drugType: 0
  colour: {r: 0.95, g: 0.55, b: 0.2, a: 1}
  description: Her own voice, about the thing in front of her. She does not know
    how she knows it.
  logText: 
  readFlag: 
  mapFloor: 
  audioClip: {fileID: 0}
  tapeLines:
  - at: 0.4
    speaker: LUCY
    text: Hand stencils are among the oldest dated pictures, hand flat on the rock,
      ochre or charcoal sprayed around it, blown,
    skipIfFlag: 
  - at: 7.6
    speaker: LUCY
    text: from the mouth or through a hollow bone, and when the hand comes away the
      outline stays.
    skipIfFlag: 
  - at: 13.64
    speaker: LUCY
    text: Chauvet, Pech Merle, tens of thousands of years old.
    skipIfFlag: 
  - at: 17.7
    speaker: LUCY
    text: Patagonia has a Cave of the Hands, hundreds, about nine thousand years,
      mostly left, the right held the pipe.
    skipIfFlag: 
  - at: 24.895
    speaker: LUCY
    text: Gargas in the Pyrenees has more than two hundred, many missing fingers,
      or folded down, nobody agrees whether that's loss or a sign.
    skipIfFlag: 
  - at: 32.095
    speaker: LUCY
    text: In 2013 somebody measured finger lengths in French and Spanish caves, I
      won't get into the method, and read about three in four as women's.
    skipIfFlag: 
  - at: 39.295002
    speaker: LUCY
    text: Most of them were women's hands.
    skipIfFlag: 
